    "dc.description.abstract" : [ {
      "value" : "Summary of Merchant Shipping Act, 2025\nAct aligns Indian shipping laws with international maritime conventions, strengthens vessel safety, environmental protection, and seafarer welfare, while promoting the development of the Indian shipping industry and ensuring ease of doing business.\nKey Provisions\n1. Registration and Regulation of Vessels\nMandatory Registration: Indian vessels must be registered in accordance with the provisions of the Act.\nSurvey and Certification: Vessels are required to undergo periodic surveys, audits, and certification to ensure seaworthiness and compliance with safety standards.\n2. Seafarer Welfare and Maritime Education\nSeafarers' Rights: Provides for the welfare, training, certification, employment, and working conditions of seafarers.\nMaritime Education: Establishes standards for maritime education and training institutions to ensure competent maritime professionals.\n3. Safety and Environmental Protection\nSafety Measures: Prescribes requirements for vessel safety, security, emergency preparedness, and accident prevention.\nPollution Control: Provides measures for the prevention and containment of pollution from vessels and establishes liability for environmental damage.\n4. Maritime Liability and Investigation\nCompensation and Liability: Lays down provisions relating to collisions, maritime claims, limitation of liability, and compensation for oil pollution damage.\nMarine Casualty Investigation: Establishes procedures for investigating marine accidents, casualties, and wrecks to improve maritime safety.",
      "language" : null,
      "authority" : null,
      "confidence" : -1,
      "place" : 0
    } ],
