    "dc.legislation.history" : [ {
      "value" : "Legislative History:\nThe Merchant Shipping Act, 2025 \n\nSource: Official Record of Parliament, India Code, and Ministry of Ports, Shipping and Waterways \n\nAct Title - The Merchant Shipping Act, 2025\nAct Number - Act No. 24 of 2025 \nAct ID (India Code) - 202524 \n Presidential Assent date - August 18, 2025 \n Enforcement Date - April 15, 2026\nNodal Ministry - Ministry of Ports, Shipping and Waterways \n\nPrecedent & Historical Rationale\n●\tOverhaul & Modernization of Legacy Maritime Laws: Repeals the sprawling Merchant Shipping Act, 1958 and the colonial-era Coasting Vessels Act, 1838, replacing 561 outdated sections with 325 streamlined clauses across 15 clean parts.\n●\tCompliance with Global Conventions & Seafarer Welfare: Codifies Indian obligations under key International Maritime Organization (IMO) and ILO conventions—including SOLAS, MARPOL, the Nairobi Wreck Removal Convention, and the Maritime Labour Convention (MLC, 2006). It expands vessel ownership eligibility (permitting OCIs, NRIs, and bareboat charters) and introduces unified \"Marine Casualty\" investigation protocols.\n \nParliamentary Trajectory & Enactment\n●\tFormulation: Introduced by the Union Minister of Ports, Shipping and Waterways, Shri Sarbananda Sonowal, as the Merchant Shipping Bill, 2024 (Bill No. 183C of 2024) to reduce compliance burdens, digitize ship registration, and support Maritime India Vision 2030.\n●\tParliamentary Passage: Introduced in the Lok Sabha on December 10, 2024; passed by the Lok Sabha on August 6, 2025; and passed by the Rajya Sabha on August 11, 2025.\n●\tPresidential Assent: Received the assent of the President of India on August 18, 2025.\n●\tEnforcement: Enforced on April 15, 2026.",
      "language" : null,
      "authority" : null,
      "confidence" : -1,
      "place" : 0
    } ],
